{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1140829-the-death-purview-and-ghost-ships-phantom-vehicles-etc","id":1140829,"title":"The Death Purview and Ghost Ships/Phantom Vehicles/Etc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-16T08:56:51-07:00","id":1140829,"title":"The Death Purview and Ghost Ships/Phantom Vehicles/Etc","content":"This has been bothering me for quite awhile, but the Death Purviews (all versions I have personally read) only mention the ghosts of human individuals, underworld guardians, undead, and very little else. But literature, folklore, history, and popular culture all mention tales of literal ghost ships, phantom vehicles, apparitions of long-destroyed buildings, etc. A Death God should be able to summon and control such things shouldn't they? This seems to be a huge missing piece to the purview. For example, need a lift? Summon a phantom vehicle derived from a fiery crash. International travel? Why not a plane shot down in a war? Need a place for a night and there's only ruins? Summon the spirit of the building and have it manifest for you and your band. Just curious as to why this hasn't been mentioned by anyone. And now that it has, would anybody incorporate this into their game? If so how would you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T09:21:48-07:00","id":1140837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1140829-the-death-purview-and-ghost-ships-phantom-vehicles-etc#post1140829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has been bothering me for quite awhile, but the Death Purviews (all versions I have personally read) only mention the ghosts of human individuals, underworld guardians, undead, and very little else. But literature, folklore, history, and popular culture all mention tales of literal ghost ships, phantom vehicles, apparitions of long-destroyed buildings, etc. A Death God should be able to summon and control such things shouldn't they? This seems to be a huge missing piece to the purview. For example, need a lift? Summon a phantom vehicle derived from a fiery crash. International travel? Why not a plane shot down in a war? Need a place for a night and there's only ruins? Summon the spirit of the building and have it manifest for you and your band. Just curious as to why this hasn't been mentioned by anyone. And now that it has, would anybody incorporate this into their game? If so how would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of destroyed objects having a reflection in an afterlife is very culturally specific. Some cultural groups will destroy objects during funerals to send them off to the afterlife with the recently deceased, that sort of thing. However, like most things, this is not a cultural constant. And, further, it is occasionally tricky to work out when objects were destroyed in funeral rituals for this reason, or as an attempt to prevent grave robbing by making all of the items interned with the dead person worthless.<br /> <br /> I do not know of any instances of Death Deities interacting with objects in this method however, while there are some vehicles that come to mind, those are more in the realm of the Psychopomp than the Death Deity. (though of course there is often some overlap between these) While it may be a common literary theme in modernity, and have a place in folklore, the mythological presence of these concepts is more limited. I would allow an up-and-coming Scion to develop powers such as these as they alter the cosmology of their Pantheon to include ideas of ghosts of destroyed objects for example, but I wouldn't build it into the baseline of the Purviews since it is mythically uncommon.<br /> <br /> Some of the proposed functions, however, I feel step on the toes of other Purviews too heavily. Summoning vehicles is well within the realm of Psychopomp or Travel Purviews. If a Scion happened to have both Death and Psychopomp/Travel, I would be totally comfortable with them fluffing their powers as calling forth a destroyed vehicle, the same way I'd be totally comfortable with a Scion who has both Water and Psychopomp/Travel pulling sunken ships as a vehicle. But, I wouldn't allow Death to be able to replicate these effects alone. Mediating transportation isn't a function of a Death Deity, Hades, for example, doesn't have any relation to the transportation of individuals or goods, while Hermes does.<br /> <br /> Similarly, calling forth a building enters into the realm of stepping on other Purviews that already have similar concepts built into them. Frost, Earth, Artistry/Forge, these Purviews are often given reign over the construction of buildings in a snap. Giving it to Death would be expanding Death conceptually into the realm of other Purviews.<br /> <br /> If a Scion came from a culture that had object-souls, I would allow them to play with this idea through Boons that manipulated mortal souls. However, for everyone else, I would be grossly unsure of allowing it. It widens Death substantially, watering down its themes, while at the same time taking functionality over from other Purviews. If I had two players, one who had Death, and one who had Psychopomp, the player who was using Psychopomp would want to be the facilitator of transportation, and if the Death Scion could do what they did, I expect they would feel somewhat disapointed and wonder why they just didn't take Death.<br /> <br /> I would allow someone to have Ghost Ships, or similar deathly-transports as a Relic though, that would be fine. But, widening the Purview so substantially, especially in a way that is mythically uncommon, and very culturally specific, I would be very unsure about. If you want to call forth transportation, take Psychopomp/Travel. If you want to magic up a sword, take Artistry. If you want an instant fortress, take Earth, Frost, Artistry, maybe even Guardian. Widening Death to encompass destroyed objects gets tricky, and plays the Purview very wide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T16:40:53-07:00","id":1140925,"title":"","content":"Will point out, that Ghost ships differ a lot, sometimes being a ghostly reflection of the ship, sometimes being a long abandoned ship that is &quot;Haunted&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T19:56:30-07:00","id":1140956,"title":"","content":"As I understand, ghost ships and the like are merely vehicles which are being haunted by, well, ghosts.<br /> <br /> Unless you're a member of the shinto pantheon, these things don't really have a soul of their own and would be difficult to qualify as a 'ghost.'<br /> <br /> Typically, a ghost is something that was once alive, died, then stuck around after its death as an immaterial spirit. How exactly do you kill a car? Do you remove the battery pack? And if so, does installing a new one count as 'resurrecting' the car?<br /> <br /> Lots of complicated questions being involved here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:05:03-07:00","id":1142688,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't this just be a use of the Marvel system? By spending extra legend and using one of the motifs you have to justify it, you can replicate powers from other purviews. <br /> <br /> Somewhere in the Ask Neall thread he mentions using Animal (Birds) to replicate a Sun boon that allows you to blind a target, justifying it as a cloud of birds that obscures vision instead of a blinding glare. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that you could pull off &quot;I spend some extra legend to mimic this Travel boon that summons a vehicle, but I'm channeling it through my Death purview so it takes the form of a ghost ship.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T18:45:28-07:00","id":1144247,"title":"","content":"Thank-you Z. i had somehow forgotten that little bit of info. Greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}